     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Most likely you didn’t run MCMC long enough and after your binning and thinning, you are left with no posterior trees. You can either let your sampling run longer\r\n or adjust the binning and thinning parameters.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Yuchao<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;MS Gothic&quot;\">雷万</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Microsoft JhengHei&quot;,sans-serif\">钧</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">leiw...@novogene.com</a>]\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Thursday, September 7, 2017 1:00 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> phylogeny &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">phyl...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;; yuchaoj &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yuc...@wharton.upenn.edu</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Canopy of problem<u